<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44801" root="&#xA;                        يقن&#xA;                    " body-key="Y1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَقِينٌ</span></b> 
                         is of the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَعِيلٌ</span> in the sense of
the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَاعِلٌ</span>, signifying <i>Sure,</i> or <i>certain,</i>
                        
and <i>manifest.</i> (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>knowledge,</i> or
<i>certainty;</i> [see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَنٌّ</span>;] <i>instinctive</i> and <i>inferential.</i> (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيْنُ اليَقِينِ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيْنٌ</span> (latter
part). ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحقُّ اليَقِينُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَقُّ اليَقِينِ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَامِعٌ</span>;
where the two words are said to have the same
meaning: and Bd and Jel in lvi. 95; in the
latter of which, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اليقين</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَقُّ اليَقِينِ</span> is expressly
said to be an epithet: see also Ham, p. 335.

 </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
